    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "MusicEvent",
      "id": "4eeeba9927541cfa",
      "title": "Με κέντρο τον Ραχμάνινοφ",
      "description": "Με κέντρο τον Ραχμάνινοφ Η διεθνώς αναγνωρισμένη ελληνο-βενεζουελανή πιανίστρια παρουσιάζει στο Μέγαρο ένα απαιτητικό ρεσιτάλ με τρεις Σονάτες για πιάνο, έργα κορυφαίων ρώσων συνθετών. Ξεχωρίζει η Πρώ",
      "fullDescription": "The Megaron Mousikis hall settles into focused silence as the orchestra takes position. The program tonight centers on Rachmaninoff — that particular Russian romantic sensibility, the piano writing that demands everything from a performer, the orchestral textures that feel like weather systems moving through the concert hall.\n\nCentering an evening on Rachmaninoff means committing to emotional architecture. His compositions don't do restraint. The piano concertos require virtuosity, but the real challenge is sustaining the emotional arc across movements that span vast territory. The Megaron's programming places his work in context, surrounded by complementary pieces that illuminate different facets of the repertoire.\n\nThe audience for classical music at Megaron brings particular expectations. These are listeners who've heard these pieces before — many times, many interpretations — and come specifically to experience this version, these performers, this evening. Scores sometimes appear on laps. Eyes close during familiar passages. The attention is intense in the way that only classical music audiences achieve.\n\nThe Megaron Mousikis provides the acoustic environment Rachmaninoff requires. Built for orchestral precision, the hall amplifies the quietest passages while handling the biggest climaxes without strain. When the piano cascades through a particularly demanding passage, the room contains the sound without collapsing it. When the orchestra swells to Rachmaninoff's characteristic peaks, the experience becomes physical.\n\nIf you want music that provides background atmosphere, that asks nothing of its listeners, this program will overwhelm you. Rachmaninoff wrote for active attention — the structures reveal themselves to those who follow them. But if you're ready to give yourself to an evening of Russian romantic piano music performed in one of Europe's finest concert halls — if you want to hear why Rachmaninoff still packs these rooms — you're in the right seats.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Thursday, February 26, 2026 |\n| **Doors** | 19:00 |\n| **Concert** | 20:00 |\n| **Venue** | Megaron Mousikis, Vasilissis Sofias & Kokkali |\n| **Getting there** | Megaro Moussikis Metro (Blue line), direct access |\n| **Price** | €15-50 depending on seating |\n\nAt the center of tonight's program: the composer who wrote for every emotion simultaneously.",
