    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "MusicEvent",
      "id": "21e99b75e6d07303",
      "title": "Η Αθήνα από την Ανατολή στη Δύση 1821-1896",
      "description": "Η Αθήνα από την Ανατολή στη Δύση 1821-1896 Πώς ήταν η Αθήνα, μια μικρή οθωμανική πόλη, στις αρχές του 20ού αιώνα; Πώς σε λιγότερο από έναν αιώνα μεταμορφώθηκε σε μια νεοκλασική πόλη που φιλοξένησε με",
      "fullDescription": "The Megaron's main hall fills with an audience carrying specific historical awareness. Tonight's program traces Athens through 75 years — 1821 to 1896, from revolutionary capital of a newborn nation to established European city. The music is the vehicle; the history is the destination.\n\n\"Athens 1821-1896\" represents programmatic ambition. The selection spans the music that accompanied the city's transformation — from the folk melodies of a recently liberated people through the classical compositions that marked Greece's entry into European cultural life. Each piece carries context: this is what Athens sounded like during the reign of Otto, during the Megali Idea period, during the first modern Olympics.\n\nThe audience for historically-themed concerts brings particular engagement. These are listeners who understand the dates referenced, who can place musical choices in political and social context. You'll find history enthusiasts alongside music devotees, each finding different entry points into the same material. The program notes become companions to the performance.\n\nThe Megaron Mousikis provides the ceremonial weight this kind of historical project requires. The main hall's capacity and acoustic excellence match the ambition of the programming. When the orchestra plays music from a specific era, the setting amplifies the sense of occasion — this is Athens now, honoring Athens then.\n\nIf you want pure musical entertainment divorced from historical narrative, this program's scholarly framework might feel constraining. The evening works best for those who want both — beautiful music and the story it tells. But if you're curious about how Athens sounded to itself during its first 75 years as a modern capital, if you want to experience musical nation-building — this is the concert that attempts that synthesis.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Friday, February 27, 2026 |\n| **Doors** | 19:00 |\n| **Concert** | 20:00 |\n| **Venue** | Megaron Mousikis, Vasilissis Sofias & Kokkali |\n| **Getting there** | Megaro Moussikis Metro (Blue line), direct access |\n| **Price** | €12-40 |\n\nSeventy-five years of a city finding its voice, performed in a hall built to carry such stories.",
      "startDate": "2026-02-27T20:00:00+03:00",
      "endDate": null,
      "type": "concert",
