    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "MusicEvent",
      "id": "4d9e2f9b3cc81cc1",
      "title": "ΜΙΡΕΛΑ ΠΑΧΟΥ & ΑΔΑΜ ΤΣΑΡΟΥΧΗΣ - ΤΑ ΝΤΟΥΕΤΑ ΤΟΥ ΕΛΛΗΝΙΚΟΥ ΚΙΝΗΜΑΤΟΓΡΑΦΟΥ",
      "description": "",
      "fullDescription": "You descend into Half Note and the dimensions embrace you. Tables close enough to the stage that you could hand the musicians a drink. The bar along one wall. The specific acoustic treatment that means nothing gets lost between performer and audience. Tonight, two Greek voices share this intimate stage.\n\nMirela Pachou and Adam Tsarouchis represent a particular strand of Greek jazz — artists who've absorbed the international vocabulary but sing in their own accent. Pachou's voice carries the influence of her Mediterranean roots into jazz phrasing. Tsarouchis brings his own approach, complementary yet distinct. Together they offer an evening of interplay that couldn't happen in larger rooms.\n\nThe Half Note crowd for a double bill like this arrives with appreciation already formed. These are listeners who follow Greek jazz specifically, who know both artists' previous work. The conversations before the show reference recordings and past performances. By the time the music starts, the room has achieved that particular focus that Half Note cultivates.\n\nSince 1979, this venue has maintained its position as Athens' essential jazz room. The intimacy isn't compromise — it's philosophy. When Pachou leans into a quiet phrase, every seat receives it. When Tsarouchis responds, the exchange happens close enough that you're almost part of the conversation. The sound system serves rather than dominates.\n\nIf you need spectacle and production values, Half Note's scale will feel limiting. The power here comes from proximity — seeing decisions made in real time, watching musicians think out loud. But if you've been waiting for Greek jazz performed by two distinct voices in a room built for exactly this kind of musical dialogue — if you understand what Half Note represents — you find yourself here.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Friday, February 27, 2026 |\n| **Doors** | 20:00 |\n| **Music** | 21:30 |\n| **Venue** | Half Note Jazz Club, Trivonianou 17, Mets |\n| **Getting there** | Akropoli Metro (Red line), 10 min walk |\n| **Price** | €15-20 table, €10-15 bar |\n| **Reservations** | Essential — book ahead, confirm same day |\n\nTwo voices, one stage, a room small enough for real conversation.",
      "startDate": "2026-02-27T22:30:00",
      "endDate": null,
